     that the claimed bound sum r^j <= X (C log j)^j would need), plus comparison with Poisson/Touchard moments.
 (B) empirical tail P(r>=t) vs t, tested against exp(-c t/log t) (claim shape) and exp(-t log(t/lambda)) (Poisson shape).
 (C) Hardy-Littlewood prediction of the falling-factorial moments via exact/Monte-Carlo singular series over j-subsets of
     exponents, growth of the average singular series with j (tests the (C log j)^j local-factor heuristic).
